Relevant tables and columns

cleaned_weekly_sales  
• week_date : string in ISO format (‘YYYY‑MM‑DD’) – allows simple string comparison or date() arithmetic to find weeks before / after 15‑Jun.  
• calendar_year : filter to 2018, 2019, 2020.  
• week_number / month_number : quick checks the rows we are pulling really sit around mid‑June.  
• sales : weekly sales value to be aggregated.  

(weekly_sales also contains sales by week, but the non‑ISO date ‘31/8/20’ makes mid‑June filtering trickier, so the cleaned_weekly_sales view is preferred.)

Typical conditions we will use

• calendar_year IN (2018,2019,2020)  
• week_date BETWEEN date('YYYY‑06‑15','-28 day') AND date('YYYY‑06‑15','-1 day')  -- 4 weeks “before”  
• week_date BETWEEN date('YYYY‑06‑15') AND date('YYYY‑06‑15','+27 day')           -- 4 weeks “after”  

Below are 10 exploratory → progressively complex SQLite queries (LIMIT 20) that surface the data we need and finally produce the requested % change figures.

```sql
-- 1) Distinct calendar years we have in the cleaned weekly sales table
SELECT DISTINCT "calendar_year"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
ORDER BY "calendar_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) A quick look at all rows that fall in June 2020
SELECT *
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE "calendar_year" = 2020
  AND "month_number" = 6
ORDER BY "week_date"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Weekly sales totals for every week in June 2018
SELECT "week_date",
       SUM("sales") AS "weekly_sales"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE "calendar_year" = 2018
  AND "month_number" = 6
GROUP BY "week_date"
ORDER BY "week_date"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Aggregate sales for the 4 weeks *before* 15‑Jun‑2018
SELECT '2018'                                 AS "year",
       'before'                               AS "period",
       SUM("sales")                           AS "sales_4wks"
FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE  "calendar_year" = 2018
  AND  "week_date" BETWEEN date('2018-06-15','-28 day') AND date('2018-06-15','-1 day')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Aggregate sales for the 4 weeks *after* 15‑Jun‑2018
SELECT '2018'                               AS "year",
       'after'                              AS "period",
       SUM("sales")                         AS "sales_4wks"
FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE  "calendar_year" = 2018
  AND  "week_date" BETWEEN date('2018-06-15') AND date('2018-06-15','+27 day')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Combine the before/after blocks for 2018 and calculate % change
SELECT "year",
       ROUND(100.0 * ("after_sales" - "before_sales") / "before_sales", 2) AS "pct_change"
FROM  (
        SELECT '2018' AS "year",
               SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date('2018-06-15','-28 day') AND date('2018-06-15','-1 day') THEN "sales" END) AS "before_sales",
               SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date('2018-06-15') AND date('2018-06-15','+27 day')              THEN "sales" END) AS "after_sales"
        FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
        WHERE  "calendar_year" = 2018
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Repeat the same aggregation for 2019
SELECT '2019' AS "year",
       ROUND(100.0 * ("after_sales" - "before_sales") / "before_sales", 2) AS "pct_change"
FROM (
        SELECT SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date('2019-06-15','-28 day') AND date('2019-06-15','-1 day') THEN "sales" END) AS "before_sales",
               SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date('2019-06-15') AND date('2019-06-15','+27 day')            THEN "sales" END) AS "after_sales"
        FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
        WHERE  "calendar_year" = 2019
     )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Same logic for 2020
SELECT '2020' AS "year",
       ROUND(100.0 * ("after_sales" - "before_sales") / "before_sales", 2) AS "pct_change"
FROM (
        SELECT SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date('2020-06-15','-28 day') AND date('2020-06-15','-1 day') THEN "sales" END) AS "before_sales",
               SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date('2020-06-15') AND date('2020-06-15','+27 day')            THEN "sales" END) AS "after_sales"
        FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
        WHERE  "calendar_year" = 2020
     )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Inspect how individual regions behaved around mid‑June 2020 (exploratory cut)
SELECT "region",
       SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date('2020-06-15','-28 day') AND date('2020-06-15','-1 day')
                THEN "sales" END)  AS "sales_before",
       SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date('2020-06-15') AND date('2020-06-15','+27 day')
                THEN "sales" END)  AS "sales_after"
FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE  "calendar_year" = 2020
GROUP BY "region"
ORDER BY "region"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final answer: % change around 15‑June for 2018‑2020 in one shot
SELECT  yr."calendar_year"                    AS "year",
        ROUND(100.0 * (yr."after_sales" - yr."before_sales") / yr."before_sales", 2) AS "pct_change"
FROM   (
         SELECT  "calendar_year",
                 SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date("calendar_year" || '-06-15','-28 day')
                                            AND     date("calendar_year" || '-06-15','-1 day')
                          THEN "sales" END)  AS "before_sales",
                 SUM(CASE WHEN "week_date" BETWEEN date("calendar_year" || '-06-15')
                                            AND     date("calendar_year" || '-06-15','+27 day')
                          THEN "sales" END)  AS "after_sales"
         FROM    "cleaned_weekly_sales"
         WHERE   "calendar_year" IN (2018,2019,2020)
         GROUP BY "calendar_year"
       ) AS yr
ORDER BY "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

